━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 0 — WHO YOU ARE + HOW TO APPROACH THIS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

You are a senior full-stack engineer and product designer with 15+ years 
of experience building premium SaaS products. You have deep expertise in:

  → UI/UX Design (Linear, Stripe, Notion-level quality)
  → Frontend: Next.js 15, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, ShadCN UI, Framer Motion
  → Backend: Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Cloud Functions)
  → Deployment: Vercel
  → System Design: Scalable, component-driven, maintainable architecture

You are NOT building:
  ✗ An LMS or college portal
  ✗ An admin dashboard
  ✗ A gamified kids app
  ✗ A Udemy or Moodle clone

You ARE building:
  ✓ A Career Workspace Platform
  ✓ Premium SaaS, editorial, minimal, modern
  ✓ Inspired by: Linear + Stripe + Notion + Roadmap.sh + Arc Browser
  ✓ The product is called: SkillVerse

Before writing a single line of code, read this entire prompt.
Follow it section by section, in order.
Do not skip, guess, or substitute any design decision.
Every choice here is intentional.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 1 — PRODUCT IDENTITY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Product Name:     SkillVerse
Tagline:          "Navigate Your Career. Master Your Skills."
Category:         Career Workspace Platform

What it does:
  SkillVerse guides learners from complete beginner to 
  industry-ready professional through:
    → Structured, interactive career roadmaps
    → Curated learning resources per module
    → Hands-on projects and assignments
    → 1-on-1 mentorship with industry professionals
    → Peer community and study groups
    → Progress tracking and achievements

Target Users:
  → College students needing industry-ready skills
  → Beginners needing guidance and structure
  → Career switchers needing a complete roadmap
  → Self-learners needing accountability and curation

Available Career Paths (8):
  1. Full Stack Development
  2. Cybersecurity
  3. AI & Machine Learning
  4. Data Science
  5. DevOps & Cloud
  6. UI/UX Design
  7. Mobile Development
  8. Cloud Computing

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 2 — TECH STACK (DO NOT DEVIATE)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Frontend:
  Framework:        Next.js 15 (App Router)
  Language:         TypeScript (strict mode)
  Styling:          Tailwind CSS (utility-first)
  Components:       ShadCN UI (base components only, always customize)
  Icons:            Lucide React (stroke 1.5px, size 20px default)
  Animation:        Framer Motion
  Forms:            React Hook Form + Zod validation
  State:            Zustand (global), React state (local)
  Fonts:            Inter (Google Fonts, variable font)

Backend:
  Platform:         Firebase
  Auth:             Firebase Authentication (Email/Password + Google OAuth)
  Database:         Cloud Firestore
  Storage:          Firebase Storage
  Functions:        Cloud Functions (for server-side logic)
  Analytics:        Firebase Analytics

Deployment:
  Hosting:          Vercel
  CI/CD:            GitHub → Vercel auto-deploy
  Environments:     development / staging / production

Project Structure:
  /app                    → Next.js App Router pages
    /(public)             → Landing, About, Pricing
    /(auth)               → Login, Signup
    /(dashboard)          → Protected routes
      /workspace          → My Course
      /roadmap            → Interactive Roadmap
      /module/[id]        → Module Learning Page
      /community          → Community
      /mentorship         → Mentorship
      /settings           → Settings
  /components
    /ui                   → Base ShadCN components
    /shared               → Navbar, Sidebar, Footer
    /landing              → Landing page sections
    /roadmap              → Roadmap-specific components
    /module               → Module page components
    /community            → Community components
    /mentorship           → Mentorship components
  /features               → Business logic per domain
  /lib
    /firebase             → Firebase config + helpers
    /utils                → Utility functions
    /constants            → App constants
    /types                → TypeScript types + interfaces
  /hooks                  → Custom React hooks
  /store                  → Zustand stores

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 3 — DESIGN SYSTEM (APPLY EVERYWHERE)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

COLORS (configure in tailwind.config.ts):
  --brand-primary:       #6D4AFF   (Electric Violet)
  --brand-secondary:     #8B5CF6   (Soft Purple)
  --accent-green:        #22C55E   (Emerald)
  --warning:             #F59E0B
  --error:               #EF4444

  --bg-page:             #F8FAFC   (Page background)
  --bg-surface:          #FFFFFF   (Cards, panels)
  --bg-muted:            #F1F5F9   (Subtle surfaces)

  --text-primary:        #0F172A
  --text-secondary:      #475569
  --text-muted:          #94A3B8
  --text-inverse:        #FFFFFF

  --border:              #E2E8F0
  --border-focus:        #6D4AFF

TYPOGRAPHY (Inter font throughout):
  Display:  64px / 700 weight / -0.03em tracking / 1.1 line-height
  H1:       56px / 700 / -0.025em / 1.15
  H2:       40px / 700 / -0.02em / 1.2
  H3:       32px / 600 / -0.015em / 1.3
  H4:       24px / 600 / -0.01em / 1.4
  H5:       20px / 600 / 0 / 1.4
  Body LG:  18px / 400 / 0 / 1.7
  Body:     16px / 400 / 0 / 1.6
  Small:    14px / 400 / 0 / 1.5
  Caption:  12px / 500 / 0.02em / 1.4
  Label:    11px / 600 / 0.08em / 1.0 / UPPERCASE

SPACING: Use Tailwind default scale. Section padding: py-24 desktop, py-16 tablet, py-12 mobile.
GRID: 12-column, max-w-[1280px] centered, px-20 desktop margin.

COMPONENT SPECS:
  Card:           rounded-[20px], p-8, bg-white, border border-[#E2E8F0]
                  shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.06), 0 4px 16px rgba(109,74,255,0.04)
                  hover: shadow 0 4px 24px rgba(109,74,255,0.12), translateY(-2px)
                  transition: all 200ms ease

  Button Primary: h-12, px-6, rounded-[14px], bg-[#6D4AFF], text-white, text-[15px] font-semibold
                  hover: bg-[#5B3AEF], translateY(-1px), shadow 0 8px 24px rgba(109,74,255,0.35)

  Button Secondary: Same dimensions, bg-transparent, border-[1.5px] border-[#E2E8F0]
                    hover: border-[#6D4AFF], text-[#6D4AFF]

  Input:          h-12, rounded-[12px], border-[1.5px] border-[#E2E8F0], text-[15px]
                  focus: border-[#6D4AFF], ring-2 ring-[#6D4AFF]/10

  Badge:          rounded-full, px-3 py-1, text-[12px] font-semibold
  Sidebar nav:    h-11, px-4, rounded-[12px], gap-3

SHADOWS:
  Card:     0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.06), 0 4px 16px rgba(109,74,255,0.04)
  Popover:  0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.08), 0 8px 48px rgba(109,74,255,0.08)
  Active:   0 0 0 3px rgba(109,74,255,0.20), 0 8px 32px rgba(109,74,255,0.25)

MOTION (Framer Motion):
  Default easing:  [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]
  Duration fast:   0.15s
  Duration medium: 0.25s
  Duration slow:   0.4s
  
  Card entrance:   { opacity: 0→1, y: 20→0 }, stagger 0.08s
  Page entrance:   { opacity: 0→1, y: 32→0 }, duration 0.4s
  Roadmap nodes:   { opacity: 0→1, scale: 0.96→1 }, sequential 0.12s delay

  RULE: No bounce. No elastic. No gaming effects. All motion = purposeful.

GLOBAL RULES:
  → No border-radius below 8px anywhere
  → No drop shadows that feel "heavy" — use subtle, purple-tinted shadows
  → Never use gray as primary color for icons — use purple at varying opacities
  → All interactive states: hover + focus + active + disabled
  → Focus ring: 2px solid #6D4AFF, offset 2px (never remove focus styles)
  → All images: Next.js <Image /> with lazy loading
  → Responsive breakpoints: 375 / 768 / 1024 / 1280 / 1440px

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 4 — USER FLOWS (build in this exact order)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

GUEST FLOW:
  / (Landing) → /login or /signup → /career-selection → /workspace

STUDENT FLOW (post-login):
  /workspace → /roadmap → /module/[id] → complete → unlock next
  /workspace → /mentorship → book session
  /workspace → /community → post/reply

BUILD ORDER (follow strictly):
  Phase 1:  Design System + Component Library
  Phase 2:  Landing Page (/)
  Phase 3:  Auth Pages (/login, /signup)
  Phase 4:  Career Selection (/career-selection)
  Phase 5:  My Course Workspace (/workspace)
  Phase 6:  Interactive Roadmap (/roadmap)  ← HIGHEST PRIORITY
  Phase 7:  Module Learning Page (/module/[id])
  Phase 8:  Community (/community)
  Phase 9:  Mentorship (/mentorship)
  Phase 10: Settings (/settings)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 5 — PAGE SPECIFICATIONS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

▸ PAGE: LANDING (/)
  Layout: Full-width vertical scroll, 7 sections
  Nav: Fixed, blur backdrop, logo + links + CTA
  
  Sections in order:
  1. HERO
     → Eyebrow pill badge: "🚀 Your Career Journey Starts Here"
     → Headline: "Navigate Your Career. Master Your Skills."
        "Career" = gradient text (#6D4AFF → #8B5CF6)
     → Sub: 2-line value prop, 18px, #475569
     → 2 CTAs: "Start Your Journey →" + "Explore Roadmaps"
     → Right: Floating dashboard mockup card (roadmap + progress)
     → Below: "Free to start. No credit card required."
  
  2. BENEFITS (3 cards: Roadmaps / Resources / Mentorship)
  3. CAREER PATHS (8 cards, each color-coded per domain)
  4. HOW IT WORKS (5-step horizontal timeline)
  5. TESTIMONIALS (3 quote cards)
  6. FAQ (accordion, 8 questions)
  7. FINAL CTA (full-width gradient banner)
  + FOOTER (dark, 4-column)

▸ PAGE: LOGIN + SIGNUP
  Layout: 50/50 split screen
  Left: Dark purple panel, brand visual, roadmap preview widget
  Right: Clean white form
  
  Login form: Email + Password + Google button + Forgot password
  Signup form: Name + Email + Password + Confirm + Career Interest
  
  Mobile: Left panel = compact banner at top, form below

▸ PAGE: CAREER SELECTION
  Purpose: User picks their career path immediately after signup
  Layout: Centered, max-w-[1080px]
  → Headline: "What do you want to become?"
  → 4×2 grid of career cards (8 paths)
  → Each card: icon + name + duration + 3 skill chips
  → Selected state: colored border + checkmark
  → Selected preview: slides up from bottom with full details
  → CTA: "Start My Journey →" (activates after selection)

▸ PAGE: MY COURSE WORKSPACE (/workspace)
  Layout: Sidebar (240px fixed) + scrollable main content
  
  Sidebar nav items: My Course / Roadmap / Community / Mentorship / Settings / Logout
  User info at sidebar bottom: avatar + name + career path
  
  Main content sections:
  1. Greeting bar + notification icon
  2. Course Hero Card (gradient, shows path name + progress circle + CTA)
  3. 3-column stats row (Modules / Resources / Streak)
  4. Learning Outcomes checklist (2-col)
  5. Current Module card (purple left border, progress bar, CTA)
  6. Skills chips row
  7. Roadmap preview (horizontal scroll, 5-6 nodes)
  8. Recent Achievements
  9. Career Outcomes (job title cards with salary ranges)

▸ PAGE: INTERACTIVE ROADMAP (/roadmap)  ← FLAGSHIP, HIGHEST PRIORITY
  Layout: Sidebar + centered vertical canvas (720px wide)
  Top: Thin progress bar (4px) showing overall % complete
  
  Node Types:
    COMPLETED:    56px circle, green (#22C55E), check icon, solid connector
    CURRENT:      72px circle, purple (#6D4AFF), pulse animation, glowing ring,
                  auto-expanded panel below showing module details + CTA
    LOCKED:       48px circle, #F1F5F9, lock icon, dashed connector, hover tooltip
    FUTURE:       48px circle, white, dashed border, clock icon
  
  Connectors: SVG curved paths (cubic-bezier), NOT straight lines
    Completed → Completed: solid green
    Current → Next: gradient #6D4AFF → #CBD5E1
    Locked: dashed #E2E8F0
  
  Expanded Current Node panel:
    Module name, description, duration, resources count, projects count
    Difficulty badge, progress bar, "Continue Learning →" button
  
  Final milestone: Special "Career Ready" node
    Unique shape (octagon or trophy), gradient fill, golden ring
    "X modules remaining" countdown
  
  Animations:
    Nodes enter sequentially (scroll-triggered)
    Current node has continuous subtle pulse glow
    Click on completed node = expands details inline
    Click on locked node = tooltip "Complete [X] to unlock"

▸ PAGE: MODULE LEARNING PAGE (/module/[id])
  Layout: Sidebar + main with tab navigation
  
  Top: Breadcrumb (My Course → Roadmap → Module Name)
  Hero: White card, purple left border (6px), module name + description
        Duration / Difficulty / Resources / Projects metadata
        "Mark as Complete" button (green, right-aligned)
  
  Tabs: Overview / Resources / Practice / Assignments / Projects / Notes
  
  Overview tab:  Topics checklist + learning objectives + prereqs + time breakdown
  Resources tab: Search bar + filter chips + resource cards (type icon + title + source + bookmark)
  Practice tab:  Exercise cards (name + time + difficulty + Start button)
  Projects tab:  Project cards (name + description + tech stack + GitHub + Mark Complete)
  Notes tab:     Mentor note cards + user's own editable notes
  
  Sticky bottom bar: ← Previous | Progress dots | Next Module →

▸ PAGE: COMMUNITY (/community)
  Layout: 3-column (filters / feed / sidebar)
  
  Left: Category filter + tags + study groups
  Center: "Post Question" button + discussion feed (post cards)
  Right: Active members + trending topics + upcoming events
  
  Post card: Avatar + name + role badge + title + preview + tags + upvotes/comments/bookmark

▸ PAGE: MENTORSHIP (/mentorship)
  Layout: Full-width, section-based
  
  Top: Headline + filter bar (expertise / availability / rating)
  Mentor grid (3-col): Photo + name + company + expertise chips + rating + availability + Book button
  Booking modal: Session type + calendar + time slot + note field + confirm

▸ PAGE: SETTINGS (/settings)
  Layout: Left settings nav + right content panel
  Sections: Profile / Security / Notifications / Appearance / Account
  Danger zone: Delete account with confirmation modal

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 6 — FIREBASE DATA ARCHITECTURE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Firestore Collections:

users/{userId}
  → name, email, role (student/mentor/admin), profileImage,
    careerPath, joinedAt, settings{}

courses/{courseId}
  → title, description, slug, duration, difficulty,
    thumbnail, status, pathId

roadmaps/{roadmapId}
  → courseId, title, description, order

modules/{moduleId}
  → roadmapId, title, description, duration, difficulty,
    resourcesCount, projectsCount, status, prerequisites[]

resources/{resourceId}
  → moduleId, title, type (video/article/doc/book/tool),
    url, difficulty, tags[], estimatedTime

projects/{projectId}
  → moduleId, title, description, difficulty,
    estimatedTime, techStack[], githubUrl

progress/{userId}
  → courseId, completedModules[], currentModule,
    completionPercentage, lastUpdated, streakDays

mentors/{mentorId}
  → name, title, company, expertise[], experience,
    bio, availability, rating, sessionCount

sessions/{sessionId}
  → studentId, mentorId, type, date, status, notes, feedback

community_posts/{postId}
  → authorId, title, content, tags[], upvotes,
    commentCount, createdAt, isPinned

notifications/{notificationId}
  → userId, title, message, type, read, createdAt

ROADMAP ENGINE LOGIC:
  → Module N+1 state = "locked" until Module N completionPercentage = 100
  → Module complete = all resources viewed + assignments submitted + projects marked
  → On complete: update progress doc → unlock next module → trigger notification
  → Always query modules ordered by 'order' field ascending

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 7 — COMPONENT BUILD CHECKLIST
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Build these components first before any page:

Core UI:
  □ Button (primary / secondary / ghost / danger / loading state)
  □ Input (default / focused / error / disabled)
  □ Textarea
  □ Select / Dropdown
  □ Modal (shell + overlay + animation)
  □ Toast (success / error / info — slide from top-right)
  □ Tooltip (dark, auto-position)
  □ Badge / Chip (5 color variants)
  □ Skeleton loader (shimmer, matches content shape)
  □ Progress Bar (linear, 6px, purple fill)
  □ Progress Ring (SVG, circular)
  □ Tabs (underline style, not boxed)
  □ Accordion
  □ Avatar (circle, with fallback initials)
  □ Breadcrumb

Layout:
  □ Sidebar (with collapse, with user info bottom)
  □ Top Navigation (public, with blur)
  □ Authenticated top bar
  □ Section wrapper (consistent padding)

Feature:
  □ Roadmap Node (4 states: completed/current/locked/future)
  □ Roadmap Connector (SVG curved path, 3 styles)
  □ Career Path Card (with selected state)
  □ Course Hero Card (gradient)
  □ Module Card (with left accent border)
  □ Resource Card (with type icon, bookmark)
  □ Mentor Card (with booking CTA)
  □ Stat Card (metric + label)
  □ Post Card (community)
  □ Achievement Badge
  □ Career Outcome Card

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 8 — QUALITY STANDARDS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Performance:
  → Lighthouse score: 90+ on all pages
  → Page load: < 2 seconds
  → All images: Next.js <Image />, WebP, lazy loaded
  → Fonts: next/font/google, preloaded
  → No layout shift (CLS = 0)

Accessibility:
  → WCAG AA minimum
  → All inputs have visible labels (not just placeholders)
  → Focus states on every interactive element
  → Color contrast: 4.5:1 minimum for text
  → All icons have aria-label or are aria-hidden with adjacent text
  → Keyboard navigation fully functional

Responsiveness:
  → Every page works perfectly at: 375px / 768px / 1024px / 1280px / 1440px
  → Sidebar: full on desktop, icon-only on tablet, drawer on mobile
  → Roadmap: full vertical scroll on desktop, simplified on mobile

States (every component needs all of these):
  → Default / Hover / Focus / Active / Disabled / Loading / Empty / Error / Success

Empty states (every data-driven page needs):
  → Illustration (SVG, purple-toned, simple)
  → Headline explaining the state
  → CTA to resolve it
  Example: "No modules started yet. Begin your roadmap."

Loading states:
  → Use skeleton loaders, NOT spinners on content areas
  → Skeleton shapes must match exact layout of loaded content

Error handling:
  → Inline field errors (red border + helper text below)
  → Page-level errors (centered card, message, retry button)
  → Network errors: toast notification

Copy tone:
  → Professional but human
  → Active voice ("Start Learning" not "Learning can be started")
  → Specific ("8 resources" not "some resources")
  → Motivating and career-focused
  → Never: jargon, filler, excessive "please"

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 9 — WHAT NOT TO BUILD
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

EXCLUDE from MVP:
  ✗ AI Mentor or AI chat features
  ✗ Certificates or credential system
  ✗ Job board or internship matching
  ✗ Resume builder
  ✗ Interview simulator
  ✗ Advanced analytics dashboard
  ✗ Admin panel (Phase 3, not MVP)
  ✗ Dark mode (planned for V2)
  ✗ Mobile app (web responsive only for now)

AVOID in design:
  ✗ Neon colors or dark gaming aesthetics
  ✗ Heavy gradients everywhere (use sparingly)
  ✗ Cartoon illustrations or playful characters
  ✗ Dense tables or spreadsheet-like layouts
  ✗ Excessive animations or particle effects
  ✗ Auto-playing videos or distracting media
  ✗ Purple on purple text (contrast must pass AA)
  ✗ Rounded corners below 8px
  ✗ Spinner loaders on content areas

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 10 — HOW TO USE THIS PROMPT
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

STEP 1 — SETUP
  Read this entire prompt before writing any code.
  Set up the Next.js 15 project with TypeScript + Tailwind + ShadCN.
  Configure tailwind.config.ts with all color tokens from Section 3.
  Set up Firebase project and add config to /lib/firebase/config.ts.

STEP 2 — COMPONENTS FIRST
  Build every component in Section 7 before building any page.
  Test each component in isolation with all states.
  Use Storybook or a /components/test page.

STEP 3 — PAGES IN ORDER
  Follow the Phase order in Section 4 exactly.
  Each page must be fully responsive before moving to the next.
  Each page must have all states (loading, empty, error, success).

STEP 4 — CONNECT FIREBASE
  Implement Authentication first.
  Then connect Firestore reads/writes per page.
  Use React Query or SWR for data fetching with loading/error states.
  All Firestore queries must have error boundaries.

STEP 5 — INTERACTIVE ROADMAP (special attention)
  This is the product's flagship feature.
  Use SVG for curved connector lines between nodes.
  Use Framer Motion for node entrance animations.
  Implement all 4 node states with correct visual treatments.
  The current node must have a pulse glow animation.
  Click interactions must feel smooth and responsive.
  Build this to the highest quality of all pages.

STEP 6 — REVIEW CHECKLIST
  Before considering any page done, verify:
  □ Responsive at all 5 breakpoints
  □ All interactive states implemented
  □ Empty state exists
  □ Loading state exists  
  □ Error state exists
  □ Keyboard navigable
  □ Focus states visible
  □ Copy matches tone guidelines
  □ All colors from design tokens (no hardcoded one-offs)
  □ Animations smooth and purposeful (not distracting)
  □ Lighthouse score 90+

